 "conclusions": [
  "Work is enormous and it is not winnable as asked. Work in Warsaw is 31,000 a month, work in Krakow 24,000, jobs in Berlin 16,000, jobs in London 12,000, work in Rome 11,000. Those are job board terms and the job boards own them. Livdar has no job inventory and no reason to be the tenth result.",
  "The Work niches Livdar could win have almost no volume, with one exception. English speaking jobs in Berlin is 40 a month, salary for a developer in Paris is zero, jobs in English in Madrid is zero. English speaking jobs in Amsterdam is 800 at a sixty cent cost per click, which is the only measured exception and it is in the one market where the niche is the mainstream.",
  "Community has almost no search demand in any language, and what it has is valuable. Language exchange in London is 150 a month at a dollar fifty a click, a language cafe in Berlin 150 at a dollar, running clubs in London 250 at seventy cents. Four of the phrasings returned zero and three returned no row at all. It is a real surface with a small search surface, which is a different thing from a surface that does not work.",
  "Sport is the quiet confirmation. Cycling routes in Warsaw 900, surfing in Cornwall 500, hiking around Barcelona 450, climbing in Warsaw 400, hiking around Berlin 400, walks near London 350, trekking near Milan 350, paddle surf in Valencia 350. Consistent mid hundreds at low difficulty in every market measured, with costs per click between twenty and seventy cents."
